pulse-active (1.1.0) unstable; urgency=low

  * Portability: new Makefile (PREFIX/DESTDIR) and generic installer that
    work on any Linux distribution; the .deb is now just one install method.
  * Source moved to src/pulse; the .deb is staged in a temporary directory.
  * New --once option and automatic quiet mode when stdout is not a terminal.
  * Fix: quiet mode no longer enters the alternate screen or prints escape
    codes into pipes.
  * Fix: busy loop (100% CPU) when stdin was not a terminal.
  * Fix: sensor/disk/battery caches never persisted (they ran in subshells).
  * Fix: GPU temperature no longer falls back to the NVMe sensor; CPU/GPU
    temperatures are read from hwmon without needing lm-sensors.
  * Fix: no more invented resolution/desktop values; real values from
    xrandr, xdpyinfo or DRM, otherwise N/A.
  * Fix: network rate is per second and ignores the loopback interface.
  * Fix: script no longer aborts without $USER, $SHELL or hostname(1).
  * Quiet output: NET now reports KB/s and the temperature field is TEMP:.

 -- Carlos Corral <corral1976@gmail.com>  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0600

